A rejected summary grid invalidates the full encoding hypothesis, not just one color choice. Before requesting another demo or retrying, preserve the failed output in a rejection ledger, then re-derive dimensions, separator/compartment mapping, and output-cell correspondence from every demo. Compare changed and unchanged compartments, including exceptions, against candidate encodings. A second grid that merely changes palette/occupancy details while retaining the unvalidated mapping is a cosmetic variant, not a new hypothesis.

